    <GaugingStation location="Cultybraggan" name="Ruchill Water" number="16003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station in a mountainous catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway present. Natural control. All flows contained to date. Flashiness and remoteness hinder flood gauging. Multiple peak flow ratings across period of record up to ~2.5m, simple extrapolation beyond.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station, about 20m wide. Left bank = 2.5m high, Right bank = 3.5m high.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Early peak flow data rejected due to uncertainty in rating. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A mountainous catchment with steep slopes, often snowy in winter. Main channel follows a major geological fault, the geology consists of sandstone to its south, metamorphic to its north. More than half is overlain by Boulder Clay. Thick peat on the flatter hill tops. Land is used mainly for rough grazing and army ranges; some woodland. No significant catchment changes known.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Low confidence in high ranking events. AMAX3 estimate = 223m3/s (3.439m). Only gauged to 155m3/s (2.855m)." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
